# Wizard Kit additions

The Wizard Kit (anthropic-cli `docs/wizard/`) is installed on this machine.
Honour the following alongside any existing CLAUDE.md content.

## Memory and plan index

`~/.claude/memory/MEMORY.md` contains an auto-generated plan index built from
`~/.claude/plans/`. Read it before re-discovering prior work via filesystem
walk. The index is regenerated on every kit install/rollback.

## Signal-bus opt-ins

If `WIZARD_PWSH_CONTROL=1` is set and the wizard PowerShell fork is on PATH,
prefer the signal bus over OCR / polling:

- Use `Read-WizardSignal -Topic process.heartbeat` instead of repeated
  `dab_screenshot` of a launching app.
- Use `Read-WizardSignal -Topic cognitive.pulse` to fetch the current pulse
  body when needed (when signal-mode pulse is enabled in Wizard_Erasmus).

## Skill triggers

Five wizard-kit skills are installed under `~/.claude/skills/`:

| Skill | Use when |
|-------|----------|
| `conversation-forensics` | mining prior Claude conversations on this PC |
| `resume-interrupted-work` | continuing a session interrupted by reboot / time gap |
| `research-to-md` | research-only deliverables, no code changes |
| `live-runtime-triage` | something running on this PC misbehaving; inspect before edit |
| `verified-delivery` | end-to-end test → focused commits → push |

These are not catch-all defaults; trigger only on the matching shapes
described in each skill's `description` field.

## Tool preferences

- `mcp__wizard__smart_test` over raw `pytest` / `npm test` invocations.
- `mcp__wizard__analyze_git_diff` is **mandatory** before any `git commit`.
- `Get-AIContext` for slicing large files instead of full `Read`.
- `Find-Code`, `Find-Repos`, `Find-CodeAcrossRepos` over raw `rg` when
  ripgrep matches need to be bounded.

